    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1012">

                <pb facs="0881" n="869" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg869"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.2231/451: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Long</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-06-15T13:00:00-04:00">June 15, 1940—1 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>73. Your 103 and 105, June 13 and 14.<anchor n="55" xml:id="d1012-f1"/>
                    Announcement in general terms of quota restrictions on schedule articles and
                    duty changes was issued by the Department this morning.<anchor n="56"
                        xml:id="d1012-f2"/></p>
                <pb facs="0882" n="870" xml:id="pg870"/>
                <p>Details will be published by Commerce as soon as possible. Please telegraph
                    immediately data on items 900 and 1086<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>, and inform
                    us whether statistics in your 103 are for 3 or 6 month quotas.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
